    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Wed, Feb 8, 2017 at 7:00 PM, Soutik Ghosal &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">soutik...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi, I am trying to plot some a continuous variable for different counties of\r<br>&gt; United States. But I couldn&#39;t use spectral color palette. I have used the\r<br>&gt; following code\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; library(maps)\r<br>&gt; library(mapdata)\r<br>&gt; library(mapproj)\r<br>&gt; library(hexbin)\r<br>&gt; library(viridis)\r<br>&gt; library(ggplot2)\r<br>&gt; library(rasterVis)\r<br>&gt; library(httr)\r<br>&gt; library(rgdal)\r<br>&gt; library(RColorBrewer)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; dat &lt;- data.frame(unique_state_county_allyears,county_eff)\r<br>&gt; names(dat) &lt;- c(&quot;state&quot;,&quot;county&quot;,&quot;county_eff&quot;)\r<br>&gt; dat$state &lt;- as.factor(dat$state)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; dat$state &lt;- state.abb[match(dat$state,<a href=\"http://state.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://state.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367366992000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CQd4uj9f0iKQUtYOuPa3V\">state.name</a>)]\r<br>&gt; dat$county &lt;- tolower(dat$county)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; county_df &lt;- map_data(&quot;county&quot;, projection = &quot;albers&quot;, parameters = c(39,\r<br>&gt; 45))\r<br>&gt; names(county_df) &lt;- c(&quot;long&quot;, &quot;lat&quot;, &quot;group&quot;, &quot;order&quot;, &quot;state_name&quot;,\r<br>&gt; &quot;county&quot;)\r<br>&gt; county_df$state &lt;- state.abb[match(county_df$state_name,\r<br>&gt; tolower(<a href=\"http://state.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://state.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367366992000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CQd4uj9f0iKQUtYOuPa3V\">state.name</a>))]\r<br>&gt; county_df$state_name &lt;- NULL\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; state_df &lt;- map_data(&quot;state&quot;, projection = &quot;albers&quot;, parameters = c(39, 45))\r<br>&gt; choropleth &lt;- merge(county_df, dat, by = c(&quot;state&quot;, &quot;county&quot;))\r<br>&gt; choropleth &lt;- choropleth[order(choropleth$order), ]\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ggplot(choropleth, aes(long, lat, group = group)) +\r<br>&gt;   geom_polygon(aes(fill = county_eff), colour = alpha(&quot;white&quot;, 1 / 2), size\r<br>&gt; = 0.2) +\r<br>&gt;   geom_polygon(data = state_df, colour = &quot;white&quot;, fill = NA) +\r<br>&gt;   coord_fixed() +\r<br>&gt;   theme_minimal() +\r<br>&gt;   ggtitle(&quot;County Effect of counties in all states and counties in the\r<br>&gt; data&quot;) +\r<br>&gt;   theme(axis.line = element_blank(), axis.text = element_blank(),\r<br>&gt;         axis.ticks = element_blank(), axis.title = element_blank()) +\r<br>&gt;   scale_fill_viridis(option=&quot;viridis&quot;,discrete=FALSE,direction=1)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; where county_eff (centered around 0) is the variable I want to plot and\r<br>&gt; unique_state_county is the data frame which has the state and county names.\r<br>&gt; Later on, I found out that if I use scale_fill_viridis I won&#39;t be able to\r<br>&gt; use color palette &quot;spectral&quot;. But I need some color scheme similar to\r<br>&gt; spectral. Can anyone please help me regarding this?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
